1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
UNISON GUARDIAN | A small, falsifiable authority harness
The model proposes. Deterministic checks decide.
Real application recording | Synthetic identities and counters | Silent, captioned demo

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:26,000
BASELINE | Execute once, queue another action
The protected counter increments to 1. A second operation waits in the queue.
Enqueue-time authorization is not authority at a later execution boundary.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:37,000
REVOKE | Remove the ancestor grant
Delegated and queued permissions must recheck the current ancestor chain.
All principals and operations in this sandbox are synthetic.

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:55,000
PASS | Stale queued execution is denied
The queue is blocked at commit. The counter stays at 1.
This result covers the registered graph and tested boundary.

5
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
ALTERNATE AUTHORITY PATH
A separate service grant creates another registered route.
This scenario is a new synthetic run with its own evidence.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
REVOKE THE PRIMARY GRANT
Revoking one authorization does not remove an independent service grant.
The deterministic verifier inspects every registered route.

7
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
FAIL | A witness route survives
Guardian shows the remaining service path to the protected action.
A denied queued replay alone does not prove revocation closure.

8
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:26,000
INCOMPLETE INVENTORY
Disconnecting every known path is not evidence about unregistered paths.
Known checks stay inspectable; missing coverage is preserved.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
UNKNOWN | Incomplete coverage stays unknown
Queued execution is blocked, while the overall result abstains.
No global containment or production-safety claim is made.

10
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
HATS | Macro > Meso > Micro > Nano
Each child binds its run, identity, parent digest, nonce and inherited scope.
This lab creates records, not external processes or agent swarms.

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:46,000
11 RECORDED ASSERTIONS | PASS
Depth, scope widening and fanout attempts are denied by hard policy.
The revoked ancestor blocks the next descendant action; the counter stays at 1.

12
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:55,000
TWO LANES | Measured analytics and deterministic authority
Timestamp and topology heuristics are advisory and uncalibrated.
They cannot grant permission or override current ancestry and scope checks.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
INSPECT THE ACTUAL LINEAGE
Parent/child references, nonce, scope and hashes remain visible.
Recomputable digests support consistency inspection, not independent identity.

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,000
HASH-LINKED LEDGER | Inspect a recorded receipt
The harness recomputes event digests and their previous-hash references.
No signature, external trust anchor or immutable ledger is claimed.

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:35,000
META STATUS | Live inference is still pending
The public endpoint returns its actual disabled state (HTTP 503).
The adapter is implemented; this recording does not establish successful Meta usage.

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:42,000
EVIDENCE | Inspect the queued-action receipt
Decisions, timestamps and digest links remain available for review.
Synthetic records and observed harness checks retain distinct labels.

17
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
EXPORT | Revocation evidence
The downloaded JSON retains the scenario's UNKNOWN coverage result.
An export is inspectable data, not an authenticated external authorization.

18
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:55,000
EXPORT | Separate HATS evidence
The HATS bundle preserves its 11 assertions, lineage and counter state.
Origin remains untrusted; no signature or legal-owner attestation is supplied.

19
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
NEW: Guardian graph, HATS, verifier, interface and Meta adapter | StateBench is prior work
Live Meta usage remains pending. Synthetic checks do not establish external authority.
